MID_Stage_Howdoyouplay: The performer will...
MID_Stage_Emotion_Joy_01: Be cheerful.
MID_Stage_Emotion_Joy_02: Show delight.
MID_Stage_Emotion_Joy_03: Beam with joy.
MID_Stage_Emotion_Anger_01: Barely conceal anger.
MID_Stage_Emotion_Anger_02: Express aggravation.
MID_Stage_Emotion_Anger_03: Seem irritated.
MID_Stage_Emotion_Sadness_01: Droop shoulders.
MID_Stage_Emotion_Sadness_02: Frown and whimper.
MID_Stage_Emotion_Sadness_03: Hold back tears.
MID_Stage_Emotion_Worry_01: Put on a worried look.
MID_Stage_Emotion_Worry_02: Have knitted brows.
MID_Stage_Emotion_Worry_03: Be ill at ease.
MID_Stage_Emotion_Laugh_01: Laugh heartily.
MID_Stage_Emotion_Laugh_02: Chortle and guffaw.
MID_Stage_Emotion_Laugh_03: Giggle with glee.
MID_Stage_Emotion_Brave_01: Project bravery.
MID_Stage_Emotion_Brave_02: Act fearless.
MID_Stage_Emotion_Brave_03: Stand tall and unafraid.
MID_Stage_Emotion_Love_01: Show tenderness.
MID_Stage_Emotion_Love_02: Gesture lovingly.
MID_Stage_Emotion_Love_03: Whisper sweet nothings.
MID_Stage_Emotion_Hate_01: Explode with hatred.
MID_Stage_Emotion_Hate_02: Go into a rage.
MID_Stage_Emotion_Hate_03: Seethe and curse.
MID_Stage_Title_ComedyA: Mascarina the Thief
MID_Stage_Plot_ComedyA: Notorious in name and deed, the daring thief Mascarina\nseems to always be a step ahead!\n\nBut when she delivers a warning to the high priest,\nsaying, "Next, I steal your holy book," a sage in the\ntemple devises a plan for the guards to conceal\nthemselves in decorative armor and ambush her.\n\nWho will win in this battle of wits between a sage and an\nintrepid thief?
MID_Stage_Cast_ComedyA_01: Thief
MID_Stage_Cast_ComedyA_02: High Priest
MID_Stage_Cast_ComedyA_03: Sage
MID_Stage_Situation_ComedyA_01_t: Enter Mascarina!
MID_Stage_Situation_ComedyA_01: The thief, played by {Variable=0}, outsmarts the\nguards and escapes.
MID_Stage_Situation_ComedyA_02_t: The Holy Book
MID_Stage_Situation_ComedyA_02: The high priest, played by {Variable=0},\nreads the thief's letter where she proclaims her\nintent to take the book.
MID_Stage_Situation_ComedyA_03_t: Triumph of the Sage
MID_Stage_Situation_ComedyA_03: The sage, played by {Variable=0}, springs a trap\nand captures the thief.
MID_Stage_Title_ComedyB: The Prize of Aureus
MID_Stage_Plot_ComedyB: A rake's debauched lifestyle lands them deep in debt and\nseparated from their family. Penniless and living in exile,\nthey run into a starving old derelict and give them a scrap\nof bread, receiving in return an old map.\n\nLo and behold, the map shows the location of the gold left\nbehind by the mage Aureus.\n\nWith their family member who'd heard rumors of\nthe gold, the rake departs in search of treasure—and a\nway to turn their life around.
MID_Stage_Cast_ComedyB_01: Old Derelict
MID_Stage_Cast_ComedyB_02: Family Member
MID_Stage_Cast_ComedyB_03: Rake
MID_Stage_Situation_ComedyB_01_t: Giving in Kind
MID_Stage_Situation_ComedyB_01: A starving vagrant, played by {Variable=0},\nreceives a scrap of bread from a rake.
MID_Stage_Situation_ComedyB_02_t: Where's the Gold?
MID_Stage_Situation_ComedyB_02: The rake's family member, played by {Variable=0},\nuses the map to search for treasure in the forest.
MID_Stage_Situation_ComedyB_03_t: Actual Treasure
MID_Stage_Situation_ComedyB_03: The rake, played by {Variable=0},\ndiscovers no gold, but does find some delicious\ngolden mushrooms.
MID_Stage_Title_ComedyC: Scandal of the Shrew
MID_Stage_Plot_ComedyC: An unconventional protagonist comes to the imperial\ncapital—they're known as the shrew, and they're looking\nfor someone.\n\nAfter long believing that their sibling had been lost at sea,\nthey recently heard rumors of a reappearance.\n\nBut the shrew's personality ends up getting in the way of\nthe search, and they start causing trouble left and right.\n\nCould their sibling be alive? Will the shrew find them?\nA comedy of errors set in the imperial capital!
MID_Stage_Cast_ComedyC_01: Shrew
MID_Stage_Cast_ComedyC_02: Tavern Owner
MID_Stage_Cast_ComedyC_03: Investigator
MID_Stage_Situation_ComedyC_01_t: Flashback at Port
MID_Stage_Situation_ComedyC_01: The shrew, played by {Variable=0}, arrives at the\nport of the imperial capital and recalls their sibling, from\nwhom they've been separated.
MID_Stage_Situation_ComedyC_02_t: After the Dust Settles
MID_Stage_Situation_ComedyC_02: The tavern owner, played by {Variable=0}, turns\nthe shrew, who had caused a ruckus, over to the temples.
MID_Stage_Situation_ComedyC_03_t: Enduring Memories
MID_Stage_Situation_ComedyC_03: The investigator, played by {Variable=0}, turns out\nto be the shrew's sibling, who had lost their memories!\nA tearful reunion ensues.
MID_Stage_Title_TragedyA: The Rending Ring
MID_Stage_Plot_TragedyA: The protagonist, the scion of a noble house, wanders\ninto the woods on a hunting trip and falls in love\nwith the child of a hermit.\n\nThe couple deepens their love through many trysts.\nThe hermit, who had once been cheated by the noble's\nhouse, secretly gives the noble a cursed ring disguised as\na betrothal ring in order to kill them.\n\nThe hermit's child attempts to take the ring back,\nbut the noble, mistaking this for a change of heart,\nthrows themself into the lake in despair...\n\nA tale of the sad fate that befalls two lovers.
MID_Stage_Cast_TragedyA_01: Noble Scion
MID_Stage_Cast_TragedyA_02: Hermit
MID_Stage_Cast_TragedyA_03: Hermit's Child
MID_Stage_Situation_TragedyA_01_t: A Forbidden Love Begins
MID_Stage_Situation_TragedyA_01: The noble, played by {Variable=0}, meets the\nhermit's child in the woods, and they fall in love.
MID_Stage_Situation_TragedyA_02_t: The Rending Ring
MID_Stage_Situation_TragedyA_02: The hermit, played by {Variable=0}, gives\nthe cursed ring to the noble scion.
MID_Stage_Situation_TragedyA_03_t: In the Next Life, Then
MID_Stage_Situation_TragedyA_03: The hermit's child, played by {Variable=0},\nputs on the ring and follows their beloved noble.
MID_Stage_Title_TragedyB: Alas! Though Triumph Echoes
MID_Stage_Plot_TragedyB: After a long period of turmoil and strife, the East and\nthe West had found temporary peace. Now, however,\nthey are on the brink of war again.\n\nSoldiers from both sides are stationed at the border\ncheckpoint. Two of them are childhood friends who come\nfrom the same village, but the conflict has drawn a new\nborder and now they must face as enemies.\n\nThey exchange words and laughter across the border.\nBut then the violence begins, and they must fight...\n\nA lament for a long-lost friendship that rekindles\nduring wartime.
MID_Stage_Cast_TragedyB_01: Western Soldier
MID_Stage_Cast_TragedyB_02: Eastern Soldier
MID_Stage_Cast_TragedyB_03: Villager
MID_Stage_Situation_TragedyB_01_t: An Indelible Friendship
MID_Stage_Situation_TragedyB_01: The Western Soldier, played by {Variable=0},\nreunites with their childhood friend, the Eastern Soldier,\nat the border.
MID_Stage_Situation_TragedyB_02_t: Trading Words for Swords
MID_Stage_Situation_TragedyB_02: The Eastern Soldier, played by {Variable=0},\nlearns of the war breaking out between East and West\nand must fight.
MID_Stage_Situation_TragedyB_03_t: Dawn After the Battle
MID_Stage_Situation_TragedyB_03: A villager, played by {Variable=0}, offers flowers\nat the quiet, deserted border after the war.
MID_Stage_Title_TragedyC: Bloodlines and Blood Feuds
MID_Stage_Plot_TragedyC: When the nation's head of state is lost in battle, a noble\nfalls into ruin. Their heir, planning to exact revenge,\npretends to be a servant and infiltrates the house of the\ngeneral who killed their parent.\n\nHowever, despite their intentions, the heir falls in love\nwith the general!\n\nThen comes news of a plan to invade their country once\nagain. The noble heir reveals their true identity and\nmakes plans to return to their home...but the general,\nwho has fallen in love with the heir, invites them to\nabandon their country and run away together!\n\nA tragic love story of a couple at the mercy of fate.
MID_Stage_Cast_TragedyC_01: Prestigious Noble
MID_Stage_Cast_TragedyC_02: Noble's Heir
MID_Stage_Cast_TragedyC_03: General
MID_Stage_Situation_TragedyC_01_t: The Day the House Fell
MID_Stage_Situation_TragedyC_01: The prestigious noble, played by {Variable=0}, fights\nthe general of an enemy country and loses their life.
MID_Stage_Situation_TragedyC_02_t: Forbidden Love
MID_Stage_Situation_TragedyC_02: The noble's heir, played by {Variable=0}, infiltrates\nenemy territory, but ends up falling in love with their\nparent's killer, the general.
MID_Stage_Situation_TragedyC_03_t: The Demise of Love
MID_Stage_Situation_TragedyC_03: After running away with the noble's heir, the general,\nplayed by {Variable=0}, is ordered to be executed.
MID_Stage_Title_OperaA: Again, to You
MID_Stage_Plot_OperaA: There was once a shepherd who worshipped a god,\nlavishing them every day with prayers. But the god gave \nthe shepherd trials to test their faith.\n\nThey lost their crops, their livestock, their savings.\nThey fell ill...\n\nStill the shepherd called out the god's name and did not\nlose faith, no matter the hardship.\n\nWhat awaited the shepherd then? A painful yet beautiful\nstory of humans and gods.
MID_Stage_Cast_OperaA_01: Shepherd
MID_Stage_Cast_OperaA_02: God
MID_Stage_Cast_OperaA_03: God's Child
MID_Stage_Situation_OperaA_01_t: Trial of the Gods
MID_Stage_Situation_OperaA_01: The shepherd, played by {Variable=0}, receives\na trial from the god and loses the crops and sheep they\nhad raised.
MID_Stage_Situation_OperaA_02_t: A Test of Faith
MID_Stage_Situation_OperaA_02: The god, played by {Variable=0}, considers what\nkind of trial to bestow upon the shepherd.
MID_Stage_Situation_OperaA_03_t: Blessings upon the Soul
MID_Stage_Situation_OperaA_03: The god's child, played by {Variable=0}, informs the\nshepherd, who has passed their trials, that they are to\nwed one another.
MID_Stage_Title_OperaB: Phantom of the Arena
MID_Stage_Plot_OperaB: Gladiators are no strangers to the specter of death.\nBut when one gladiator was cut down, they returned to\nthe arena as a literal ghost—known as the phantom.\n\nThe protagonist, a young gladiator, meets this phantom\nand receives a black sword, and their fame grows with\neach victory.\n\nHowever, as the gladiator's popularity grows, they\nbecome arrogant—until, during the final battle to\ndetermine the winner, the black sword breaks...\n\nA bloody, bizarre tale that lurks in the shadows of glory\nand failure!
MID_Stage_Cast_OperaB_01: Young Gladiator
MID_Stage_Cast_OperaB_02: Rival Gladiator
MID_Stage_Cast_OperaB_03: Phantom
MID_Stage_Situation_OperaB_01_t: Phantom of the Arena
MID_Stage_Situation_OperaB_01: The young gladiator, played by {Variable=0},\nreceives a black sword from the phantom, and their\nwinning streak continues.
MID_Stage_Situation_OperaB_02_t: Glory's End
MID_Stage_Situation_OperaB_02: The rival gladiator, played by {Variable=0}, defeats\nthe arrogant young gladiator.
MID_Stage_Situation_OperaB_03_t: Cycle of Darkness
MID_Stage_Situation_OperaB_03: The phantom, played by {Variable=0}, takes the\nblack sword and, looking contented, seeks another\ntarget to curse.
MID_Stage_Title_OperaC: Rainbows over Iapetus
MID_Stage_Plot_OperaC: The Iapetus Mountains are a sacred mountain range\nin northern Dagda. Numerous spirits reside there and\nare said to appear before humans during rainbows.\n\nA woodcutter climbs the mountains during a rainbow,\nand the spirits guide them to the spirit sovereign.\n\nJust as they consider their fortune, they learn they\nare to be tried as a criminal who destroyed the area.\n\nA fantasy of humans and spirits, shining with all the\ncolors of the rainbow.
MID_Stage_Cast_OperaC_01: Tree Spirit
MID_Stage_Cast_OperaC_02: Spirit Sovereign
MID_Stage_Cast_OperaC_03: Woodcutter
MID_Stage_Situation_OperaC_01_t: The Spirits' Trial
MID_Stage_Situation_OperaC_01: The tree spirit, played by {Variable=0}, charges\nthe woodcutter with chopping down their friends.
MID_Stage_Situation_OperaC_02_t: The Verdict
MID_Stage_Situation_OperaC_02: The spirit sovereign, played by {Variable=0},\naccepts the charges and tries to punish the woodcutter.
MID_Stage_Situation_OperaC_03_t: To Save and Be Saved
MID_Stage_Situation_OperaC_03: The woodcutter, played by {Variable=0}, is\nprotected by the spirits of animals they had saved in the\npast, and makes their way safely home.
MID_Stage_Title_SpecialA: Rise of the White-Maned Demon
MID_Stage_Plot_SpecialA: The Rise of the White-Maned Demon, one of Dagda's\ngreatest literary masterpieces, finally comes to the stage!\n\nA young general, framed by his best friend, is on the\nverge of being executed when he is saved by Mars,\nthe Bringer of War. He must undertake a trial in the\narena and becomes known as the White-Maned Demon.\n\nBattles with powerful foes, traps set by his enemies,\nlove and separation from a beautiful priest...\n\nEven now, the White-Maned Demon continues to face\nhardships, until the day comes when he can finally\nprove his innocence and seize his freedom.
MID_Stage_Cast_SpecialA_01: Young General
MID_Stage_Cast_SpecialA_02: General's Friend
MID_Stage_Cast_SpecialA_03: Gladiator
MID_Stage_Cast_SpecialA_04: Priest
MID_Stage_Cast_SpecialA_05: White-Maned Demon
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialA_01_t: Young General's Advance
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialA_01: The young general, played by {Variable=0},\ncontributes greatly on the battlefield.
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialA_02_t: Baseless Accusations
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialA_02: The general's friend, played by {Variable=0}, \nentraps the general and has him imprisoned as a criminal.
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialA_03_t: The White-Maned Demon
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialA_03: A gladiator, played by {Variable=0}, fights the\ngeneral, who is now the White-Maned Demon, and gets\nmercilessly defeated.
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialA_04_t: A Captivating Afternoon
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialA_04: The priest, played by {Variable=0}, meets the\nWhite-Maned Demon in secret in prison.
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialA_05_t: Victory for Tomorrow
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialA_05: The White-Maned Demon, played by {Variable=0},\ntriumphs over a formidable foe despite a despicable trap.
MID_Stage_Title_SpecialB: Seven Labors of Arago
MID_Stage_Plot_SpecialB: The hero Arago, a human born to Divine Emperor Dagda,\nwas renowned throughout Dagda, not only for his valor\nbut also for his many romantic entanglements. Now, the\nsaga of Arago's heroic deeds will be passionately\nperformed on stage!\n\nFrom his extermination of the giant sandbael, to his duel\nwith the chief of the Lydians, to his crossing of the\nmountain pass with the beautiful Olivia, to his battle to \nuphold his vow to the king of Brigid—it is all retold here!\n\nPrepare to witness history.
MID_Stage_Cast_SpecialB_01: Villager
MID_Stage_Cast_SpecialB_02: Lydian Chief
MID_Stage_Cast_SpecialB_03: Olivia
MID_Stage_Cast_SpecialB_04: Enemy Chief
MID_Stage_Cast_SpecialB_05: Arago
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialB_01_t: Exterminating the Monster
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialB_01: After Arago defeats the giant sandbael, the villager,\nplayed by {Variable=0}, showers him with praise.
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialB_02_t: Duel of the Century
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialB_02: The Lydian chief, played by {Variable=0},\nchallenges Arago to a duel, but struggles to oppose him.
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialB_03_t: A Romantic Encounter
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialB_03: Olivia, played by {Variable=0}, has her heart stolen\nby the coarse but strong Arago.
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialB_04_t: A Prodigious Alliance
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialB_04: The enemy chief, played by {Variable=0}, is\ndefeated and disgraced by Arago and the king of Brigid.
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialB_05_t: The Endless Legend
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialB_05: Arago, played by {Variable=0}, sets off toward his\nnext battle in search of a new enemy.
MID_Stage_Title_SpecialC: The Matchless Cohen
MID_Stage_Plot_SpecialC: The story of peerless bard Cohen—a prodigy whose name\nis known by all!\n\nCohen traveled all over Dagda with vihuela in hand,\ncomposing and performing songs of all kinds, leaving\nlegend after legend in his wake. It is said that with his\nmusic, he drove away a rat infestation and turned a\nbarrel of water into mellow ghosh. Indeed, legend has it\nthat the man's playing once moved a mountain!\n\nThis illustrative performance recounts his moving\nlife story, from his promising youth to his tragic downfall.
MID_Stage_Cast_SpecialC_01: Cohen
MID_Stage_Cast_SpecialC_02: Villager
MID_Stage_Cast_SpecialC_03: Temple Soldier
MID_Stage_Cast_SpecialC_04: Ruffian
MID_Stage_Cast_SpecialC_05: Kalla
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialC_01_t: A Young Singer's Troubles
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialC_01: Cohen, played by {Variable=0}, considers whether\nhe is capable of an even more enticing performance.
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialC_02_t: The Enchanting Performer
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialC_02: A villager, played by {Variable=0}, sings the praises\nof Cohen's skill with the vihuela.
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialC_03_t: When the Wind Blows
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialC_03: A soldier at a temple, played by {Variable=0},\nis emboldened by Cohen's song, their morale increased.
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialC_04_t: Life-Giving Water
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialC_04: A ruffian, played by {Variable=0}, is in high spirits\nwhen water is turned to ghosh by Cohen's performance.
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialC_05_t: May His Melody Be Eternal
MID_Stage_Situation_SpecialC_05: Kalla, played by {Variable=0}, mourns the loss\nof Cohen, her sorely missed son.
